# AI Integration Rules

- Call Groq only from server-side code.
- Keep API credentials in environment variables.
- Use structured output where supported.
- Validate model output with Zod.
- Treat model output as untrusted input.
- Ask follow-up questions when required trip information is missing.
- Do not allow AI to invent flight offers, availability, prices, taxes, or point balances.
- Do not use AI as the source of truth for numerical savings.
- Use deterministic application code for optimization and ranking.
- Use AI to explain recommendations based only on verified provider data.
- Handle malformed output, timeouts, and model errors.
- Keep prompts focused and avoid sending unnecessary personal data.
